---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import "bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css";
---
<Layout title='Weekday Schedule for the Perno Family'>
  <main>
    <h1>Schedule</h1>
    <p>The following schedule is an approximation. Always follow the kid's signs first and foremost, but this can be a helpful guide.</p>

		<table class="table">
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<th>~7:00am</th>
					<td>Wake up</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>7:30-9:30am</th>
					<td>Breakfast</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>11:00am</th>
					<td>Lunch</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>12:00-2:00pm</th>
					<td>Nap / Quiet Time</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>2:30pm</th>
					<td>Snack</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>6:00pm</th>
					<td>Dinner</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>7:00pm</th>
					<td>Story Time</td>
					<td>Daniel gets an 8 oz bottle of whole milk around this time too</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<th>7:30pm</th>
					<td>Bedtime</td>
					<td></td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	
		<h3>Daniel's Bedmates</h3>
		<p>He is old enough to have stuffies in his bed now, although he doesn't really care about them. <strong>Avoid strangulation hazards</strong>, like loose sheets or blankets. Pillows are unnecessary and potentially hazardous too.</p>
  
		<h3>TV</h3>
		<p>Try to limit TV to under two hours a day, prioritizing slower paced, less stimulating shows (e.g. Daniel Tiger, Sesame Street, Arthur). Too much TV&mdash;especially overstimulating content&mdash;can exacerbate behavioral issues and worsen sleep quality.</p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
	h1 {
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	body { background-color: unset; }
	main {
		margin: auto;
		padding: 1em;
		max-width: 80ch;
	}
	.table>:not(caption)>*>* { /* overwrite bootstrap style */
		background-color: unset;
	}
	.list-unstyled {
		padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
	}

	.text-center {
		text-align: center;
	}
	p {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}
</style>